      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before becoming part of Detroit, the land that is now Chandler Park belonged to Grosse Pointe Township until the city annexed it in 1917.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.detroit1701.org/Chandler%20Park.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After World War I, Detroit earmarked Chandler Park for development, making it one of the city\u2019s first major park projects.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.detroit1701.org/Chandler%20Park.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Wayne County opened a large aquatic center in Chandler Park in 1998, a facility that remains well\u2011maintained today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
